@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# ai.desertant:align
+
+Word-timestamp refinement for Android: pass the words any transcriber gave you
+and the audio they came from, and get the same words back with corrected start
+and end times. The full model page is [docs/models/align.md](../../docs/models/align.md).
+
+The AAR carries one Swift JNI library per ABI (`libAlignAndroid.so`, arm64-v8a
+and x86_64). LiteRT comes from `ai.desertant:core`, which this artifact depends
+on, so use it with the same version of core as every other `ai.desertant:*`
+model in the app.
+
+## Usage
+
+```kotlin
+import ai.desertant.align.Align
+import ai.desertant.align.WordTiming
+
+val align = Align(context)                      // or Align(context, "/path/to/model/dir")
+val words = listOf(WordTiming("hola", 0.40, 0.71), WordTiming("mundo", 0.80, 1.30))
+val fixed = align.refine(samples, 16_000.0, words, "es")   // suspend; runs off the main thread
+fixed.forEach { println("${it.text} ${it.start}-${it.end} refined=${it.refined}") }
+align.close()
+```
+
+- `Align(context: Context, directory: String? = null)`: construction is cheap. The model loads on the first `refine` or on `download()`.
+- `fun isDownloaded(): Boolean`: whether the model is usable with no network.
+- `suspend fun download()`: fetch the pinned revision into the app cache (or `directory`). A no-op once present.
+- `suspend fun refine(samples: FloatArray, sampleRate: Double, words: List<WordTiming>, languageCode: String): List<WordTiming>`: mono float samples at any rate (16 kHz avoids a resample). Returns the same words, in order and with your text, with `start`/`end` replaced and `refined` set. `refined = false` means the word kept its input times (unsupported language, or a correction that was not structurally safe).
+- `Align.LANGUAGES` / `Align.isSupported(code)`: de, en, es, fr, it, ja, ko, pt, zh. The code's first two letters are used (`"pt-BR"` is `pt`); anything else passes through unchanged.
+- `close()`: release the native model.
+
+Bad input (empty audio, a non-positive rate, a time that is not finite or is outside -1 to 10,000,000 s) throws `IllegalArgumentException`; a native failure throws `AlignException`.
+
+### Unicode
+
+The model's lexical features are the UTF-8 bytes of each word in Unicode NFC,
+the form it was trained on. The Android core has no NFC of its own (it links no
+ICU), so this SDK composes every word with `java.text.Normalizer` (`Form.NFC`)
+before handing it to the core, and the core uses those bytes as they are. A
+decomposed `"café"` and a composed `"café"` therefore refine
+identically, and the text you get back is your own, unchanged.
+
+## Offline use
+
+Point `directory` at a folder that already holds the model and nothing is
+downloaded. On Android the folder must contain exactly these files from the
+Hugging Face repo [`desert-ant-labs/align`](https://huggingface.co/desert-ant-labs/align/tree/v1.1.0)
+at revision **`v1.1.0`** (the revision this SDK pins):
+
+| File | What it is |
+| --- | --- |
+| `align-coarse.tflite` | Coarse cascade stage (LiteRT) |
+| `align-fine.tflite` | Fine cascade stage (LiteRT) |
+| `refiner_config.json` | Frontend geometry, language table, cascade widths |
+| `mel_filters.bin` | Log-mel filter bank |
+| `calibrator.bin` | Correction calibrator |
+
+The `.mlmodelc` directories in the same repo are the Apple build and are not
+needed. Put the five files flat in the folder, with no `.dal-meta` directory
+beside them: that marker means "downloaded by the SDK" and makes the folder be
+checked against the manifest the SDK wrote, instead of being adopted as is. (A
+folder the SDK downloaded into itself, `.dal-meta` and all, also works offline
+afterwards.) One way to fetch the set:
+
+```bash
+for f in align-coarse.tflite align-fine.tflite refiner_config.json mel_filters.bin calibrator.bin; do
+  curl -fL -o "$f" "https://huggingface.co/desert-ant-labs/align/resolve/v1.1.0/$f"
+done
+```
+
+The SDK's license check never blocks a model from loading; with no network it
+simply retries later.
